messages.content:
{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your MMS issue. To get started, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. I have your account details. To help you with your MMS issue, could you please confirm if you are able to make regular calls and use mobile data (for example, browsing the web) on your phone right now? This will help me determine if the issue is specific to MMS or related to your overall service."
}

{
  "message": "Great question! To check if you can make regular calls, please try calling any number (like a friend or your voicemail) to see if the call goes through. For mobile data, try opening a web browser or any app that uses the internet (with Wi-Fi turned off) to see if you can access websites or online content. If you encounter any issues with either, please let me know what happens. If both work, let me know as well so I can continue troubleshooting your MMS issue."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please turn off Airplane Mode on your phone. Once it is off, check if you have cellular service and try making a call or using mobile data again. Let me know if you are able to make calls and use mobile data, or if you still experience any issues. This will help us continue troubleshooting your MMS problem."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. Since you are connected to a 2G network, this may be the reason why MMS is not working, as 2G networks are generally not suitable for MMS. Let's try switching your phone's network mode to prefer 4G or 5G, which should improve your connectivity and allow MMS to work. Would you like instructions on how to change your network mode, or can you do this on your own?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating your network mode and letting me know about your signal. Since you still can't send MMS, the next step is to check your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings, as incorrect APN settings are a common cause of MMS issues. Could you please check your APN settings and let me know if you see an MMSC (Multimedia Messaging Service Center) URL listed? If you're unsure how to check, I can guide you through the process."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your APN details. The APN name and MMSC URL you listed appear to be in the correct format, but sometimes issues can still occur if there are hidden errors or other settings are incorrect. The next step is to reset your APN settings to the default values, which often resolves MMS problems. Would you like instructions on how to reset your APN settings, or can you do this on your own?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience and for following the previous steps. Since you have already reset your APN settings, restarted your phone, and ensured you have a strong 5G signal with mobile data enabled, let's check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your device. Sometimes, having Wi-Fi Calling turned on can interfere with MMS. Could you please check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled? If it is, try turning it off and then attempt to send an MMS again. Let me know the result, or if you need instructions on how to check or disable Wi-Fi Calling."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that Wi-Fi Calling is off. The next step is to check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send and receive MMS, specifically access to storage and SMS. Please check your messaging app's permissions and ensure both 'storage' and 'SMS' permissions are enabled. If you need instructions on how to check or update app permissions, let me know."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. I checked your line and it appears you have used 15.1GB of data this month, which is slightly over your plan's 15GB data limit. When your data limit is reached, mobile data—including MMS—will stop working. To restore MMS and data, you can add more data (refuel) to your line for a small fee per GB. Would you like to add more data now? If so, please let me know how much (up to 2GB) you would like to add. The cost is $2.00 per GB."
}

{
  "message": "2GB of data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. Your mobile data and MMS should now work again. Please try sending an MMS message. If you still experience any issues, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS is working again! If you have any more questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}
